userContent.text:
Build an interactive figure using SVG.js.

CONCEPT: A Fibonacci heap is a circular doubly linked list of min-heap-ordered trees; the abstract tree picture and the explicit pointer picture describe the same structure, and the pointer view is what makes insertion O(1).
KEY INSIGHT (what students should walk away understanding): Because the root list and every sibling list are circular and doubly linked, adding a tree is just four pointer assignments and one key comparison — the heap stays deliberately messy so that insertion costs O(1).
DEMO STEPS: 7 guided steps — implement the step player in #ui

